  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> be the foot of perpendicular from the point<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math> on the line passing through the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Then the distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> from the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is",
    "image": null
  },
